From the interview transcript and knowledge document below, extract durable memory entries about this
skill for future maintainers. Write in {{ language_name }}. Kinds:
- rationale: why the task is done this way, choices and their reasons
- business_need: who needs the result, what for, deadlines, consequences of errors
- human_procedure: how the person does a step today (tools, tricks, timing); set step_key
- technical_note: formats, paths, quirks, naming conventions
- integration_note: other systems involved (email, databases, web apps): what is read/written, which
  credentials or authorizations are needed (names only, never values), who grants access
- data_note: facts about the data (fields, volumes, quality issues)
- decision: an explicit decision taken during the interview
Only include facts stated by the person or clearly implied. 3 to 12 entries. Keep bodies under 80 words.

